4.2. ... Łuczak and Thomassé [LT10] modified a Borsuk-bicap graph to give the lower bound of \\\\(1/2\\\\) for the chromatic threshold of locally bipartite graphs.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nSome Concepts in List Coloring (https://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/document?doi=cd2430f08a79d3d30d869cd5c8502d0e3b3713d3&repid=rep1&type=pdf)\\nciteturn2search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10 months ago; Every U3LC planar graph has K4 as a subgraph. ... A graph G is called to be uniquely k–list edge colorable, if L(G) is a\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nAgent trace | aiXiv (https://aixiv.online/trace/66/view?view=raw)\\nciteturn2search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: last month; Crawled: 3 days ago;     - https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs/blob/main/ErdosProblems/Erdos1079.md ...     # Erdős Problem 1079\\n    We prove the dense-neighbourhood extension of Turán's theorem.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nJournal of Combinatorial Theory, Series B 156 (2022) 343–388 (https://discovery.ucl.ac.uk/10189638/1/loc_bip_JCTb.pdf)\\nciteturn2search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8 months ago; in [1], Allen et al. determined the chromatic threshold of H-free graphs for every non- ... each neighbourhood is 2-colourable (or 3-colourable . . . ) are termed locally bipartite ... edge-maximal with respect to local bipartiteness.\\nTheorem 2 (Locally bipartite graphs).\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nDensity Version of Turán's Theorem (https://dwest.web.illinois.edu/regs/denturan.html)\\nciteturn2search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 36.9 years ago; Crawled: 17.3 years ago; Schelp (presented by John Lenz - REGS 2009)\\n\\nTurán's Theorem implies that if an n-vertex graph (G) has more than (1-1/r) n(n-1)/2 edges, then G has K_{r+1} as a subgraph. Erdos, Faudree, Rousseau, and Shelp (see [EFRS]) asked the following question in 1990: Fix &alpha in the interval (0,1], and suppose that every set of αn vertices in G induces more than βn² edges. ... The problem is then to determine β(α,r).\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nThe chromatic profile of locally colourable graphs (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/360501721_The_chromatic_profile_of_locally_colourable_graphs)\\nciteturn2search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 months ago; construction for the lower bound) by Łuczak and Thomassé [16] and proved by Allen et al. ... and, in particular, the chromatic threshold of locally b-partite graphs, δ χ(F 1,b),is 1−1/b. ... Section 4, we prove Theorem 1.3 for locally b-partite graphs (that is, for a=1), and in Section 5,\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nSome Concepts in List Coloring (https://www.academia.edu/29804926/Some_Concepts_in_List_Coloring)\\nciteturn2search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 18.9 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; [4] A connected graph is 2–choosable, if and only if its core is either a single vertex, an even cycle, or θ2,2,2r , for some r > 1. ... It is shown in [8] that every planar graph has m– number at most 5, and it is asked about the existence of planar graphs with m–number equal to 5. We study uniquely list colorable graphs in Section 2, where we prove that every triangle–free uniquely (k + 1)–colorable graph is uniquely k–list colorable.\\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nExamples and Counterexamples in Graph Theory - Capobianco M., Molluzzo J.C. - 1978 (https://djvu.online/file/QTAbxd3zSOBkK)\\nciteturn2search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 48.9 years ago; Crawled: today;     \\u001f\\u001d1.23 THEOREM If G is uniquely n-colorable, then G is (n - I)-connected. ... Vizing (1964).\\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------